<title>USA: RJR Nabisco Q3 shr rises.</title>
<headline>RJR Nabisco Q3 shr rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr		 $0.66		    $0.56</p>
<p> Net		 225,000		  216,000</p>
<p> Sales	     4,349		    4,063</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  327,710		  329,918</p>
<p>	  Nine months</p>
<p> Shr		 $1.13		    $1.45</p>
<p> Net		 396,000		  567,000</p>
<p> Sales	     12,438		   11,684</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  330,085		  329,603</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: First Call earnings estimate for the quarter was $0.67 per share.  </p>
<p>Current third quarter figures in the table exclude $8 million or $0.02 per share in after-tax restructuring charges. Year-ago third quarter figures includes an after-tax extraordinary charge of $16 million, or $0.05 per share, related primarily to the redemption by Nabisco of $409 million of debt.  </p>
<p>Excluding extraordinary expenses, net income for the third quarter was $0.68, up from $0.61 per share recorded in the year-ago period.</p>
</text>
